{'id': 2065730, 'url': 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/hr/recruiter-2065730', 'title': 'Recruiter', 'company_name': 'National Service Bureau', 'company_logo': 'https://remotive.com/job/2065730/logo', 'category': 'Human Resources', 'tags': ['microsoft office', 'time management', 'insurance'], 'job_type': 'full_time', 'publication_date': '2025-09-26T08:56:06', 'candidate_required_location': 'USA', 'salary': 'usd 24 - 29 per hour', 'description': '<p>&lt;div class="benefits"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;Dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;Health insurance&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;Vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="trix-content"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
&lt;figure class="attachment attachment--preview"&gt;&lt;img src="https://cpats.s3.amazonaws.com/system/images/536345/original/NationalServiceBureau_Logo.png" width="2120" height="359"&gt;&lt;figcaption class="attachment__caption"&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GROW WITH US!&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;National Service Bureau&lt;/strong&gt; (NSB) is looking for an outstanding &lt;strong&gt;experienced Recruiter&lt;/strong&gt;!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Recruiter Job Description:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full cycle recruiting process (job postings, sourcing, screening, interviewing, and hiring).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers to understand role requirements and develop effective recruitment strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screen resumes and conduct initial phone interviews to assess qualifications and fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and schedule interviews between candidates and hiring teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Recruiter Job Description:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We are seeking a new team member who demonstrates a high level of professionalism, attention to detail and time management skills. We also look for:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least two years of related experience\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be engaged proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of integrity and empathy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive, team-oriented attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent computer and typing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office, especially Word and Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Remote Requirements:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Not hiring in the following states: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NY, TX, PA, DC, MA, CT, ME, VT, CO, MT, CA, OR, MD&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Secure home office consisting of:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicated high-speed Internet (Cable, DSL, Fiber) with access via a hardwired connection (not wi-fi)\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internet speed required to be at 100 Mbps down, 10 Mbps up, and Latency of 100 ms or below&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Please note that &lt;strong&gt;T-Mobile Home 5G Internet is not supported&lt;/strong&gt; for our remote work environment due to performance and reliability concerns.\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedicated space where others cannot hear voice conversations, is free from background noise and other distractions (ex. Office space, extra bedroom, etc.)\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and professional backdrop\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;\xa0 Benefits include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hourly rate of $24 - $29&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monday thru Friday schedule, 8am to 5pm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company sponsored 401(k) plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, Vision Insurance with employer contributions\xa0&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company provided EAP (Employee Assistance Program)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;NSB Culture &amp; Environment:&lt;/strong&gt;\xa0&lt;br&gt;NSB is a local company focused on Insurance Subrogation and Accounts Receivable Management that has grown for over 35 years to become a leading national agency.\xa0 Our diverse and friendly team provides for a positive work environment.\xa0 We benefit from great work/life balance and are growing our team with people who are self-motivated, accountable and engaged in personal growth.\xa0&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote position.&lt;/p&gt;</p><img src="https://remotive.com/job/track/2065730/blank.gif?source=public_api" alt=""/>'}

{'id': 2052049, 'url': 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/software-dev/full-stack-engineer-2052049', 'title': 'Full Stack Engineer', 'company_name': 'Dbrand', 'company_logo': 'https://remotive.com/job/2052049/logo', 'category': 'Software Development', 'tags': ['CSS', 'graphql', 'html'], 'job_type': 'full_time', 'publication_date': '2025-08-29T00:50:59', 'candidate_required_location': 'Canada', 'salary': '$115,000 - $140,000 / year', 'description': '<div><!--block--><strong>TL;DR:</strong></div><pre><!--block-->.human[role="code"][aria-current="true"] {
​ ​ .job:last-of-type {
​ ​ ​ ​ .role { position: fixed; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .manager { content: 'self' !important; right: 100%; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .team { isolation: isolate; transition: all ease-out; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .opinion { justify-self: end; speak: none; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .growth { transform: scale(-1); }
​ ​ ​ ​ .mental-state { break-inside: avoid; }
​ ​ }

​ ​ &amp;:focus {
​ ​ ​ ​ counter-reset: stale-days;
​ ​ ​ ​ will-change: position;
​ ​ ​ ​ .worries-and-excuses { clear: both; }
​ ​ }
}

@layer utilities {
​ ​ .dbrand-career {
​ ​ ​ ​ .challenge-variety { range: infinite; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .modern-stack { outline: solid; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .supportive-team { border: none; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .continuous-learning { transition: all ease-in; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .growth { max-height: none; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .free-drinks { color: #c0ffee; }
​ ​ ​ ​ .work-hours { flex: 80%; }
​ ​ }
}

.human[role="switch"] {
​ ​ @apply dbrand-career;
}</pre><br><br><div class="h3">The Characteristics</div><ul style=""><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Curious:</strong> You’re eager to learn new concepts and master new skills. There’s no tool that’s useless in your arsenal.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Innovative:</strong> You thrive when facing new challenges and complex problems, and manage to often develop not just one but multiple solutions.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Enthusiastic:</strong> You exhibit a contagious passion for using the right technologies that are optimal to serving the needs of the end user.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Disciplined:</strong> You never allow the details to slip, understanding that every bit of minutiae forms the bigger picture.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Persistent:</strong> You’ve never failed. You’ve only experienced speed bumps on your path to success.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Reliable:</strong> You live up to both verbal and written agreements. You can be trusted to work effectively, without oversight.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Perfectionist:</strong> You persist until the smallest detail has been optimized.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Agile:</strong> You’re nimble. You’re adaptable.\xa0</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Collaborative:</strong> You enjoy purposeful teamwork. You value the contributions and perspectives of your colleagues as much as those of your CEO.</li></ul><br><br><div class="h3">The Responsibilities and Qualifications</div><div><!--block-->In order to make a positive impact as part of our team, your focus in this role will be to:</div><ul style=""><li style=""><!--block-->Develop thoughtful, responsive, and accessible web experiences.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Collaborate with our internal design team and maintain intuitive, responsive user interfaces with a focus on front-end technologies and accessibility.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Contribute to the selection and integration of appropriate technologies for web development projects.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Integrate with external APIs and ensure seamless operations.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Perform code reviews for quality and security, and to maintain high code quality standards.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Engage in design and architecture discussions, and contribute to technical decision-making processes.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Continuously improve our developer experience.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Ensure automated test coverage and web service availability.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Participate actively in coding communities, and stay informed about emerging technologies and trends, and adhere to best practices for code maintainability, accessibility, and performance.</li></ul><div><!--block-->The successful candidate should have proficiency in the following:\xa0</div><ul style=""><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Languages:</strong> TypeScript, CSS, HTML, basic experience in other scripting languages (e.g. Python, Bash).</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Web Frameworks:</strong> SvelteKit; experience with other JavaScript frameworks such as Next.js, Solid, Remix, or Nuxt is considered an asset.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>UI Libraries:</strong> Some experience with Svelte/React/Vue, particularly for custom internal components.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>TypeScript:</strong> Strong knowledge and proficiency, including ES2022 features, Types/Interfaces, Generics and Conditional Types.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>HTML:</strong> Proficient in HTML5, experienced in writing accessible and SEO-friendly markup, and familiar with modern elements and Web APIs.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>CSS:</strong> High proficiency in modern CSS, including CSS Grid, CSS Custom Properties, modern best practices, and Tailwind.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Backend Environments</strong>: Familiar with serverless, edge, and Node.js runtimes.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>APIs</strong>: Proficiency with GraphQL and JSON REST APIs, including related tools for code generation and type completion.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Content Management</strong>: Experience working with headless CMSs and other data sources.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Repository Management</strong>:<ul style=""><li style=""><!--block-->Solid experience working with git and GitHub.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Basic understanding of pnpm and working in monorepos.</li></ul></li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>CI/CD:</strong> Experience with GitHub Actions.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Testing:</strong> Writing and automating tests, such as unit, snapshot, and integration tests.</li><li style=""><!--block--><strong>Soft Skills</strong>:<ul style=""><li style=""><!--block-->Ability to communicate effectively with non-technical stakeholders.</li><li style=""><!--block-->Continual learning and improvement in testing methodologies and other areas of expertise.</li></ul></li></ul><br><br><div class="h3">The Moment of Truth </div><div><!--block-->The total compensation package for this role includes a competitive base salary, a comprehensive suite of benefits, and inclusion in our profit sharing and GRSP programs. While our HQ is located a few minutes west of Toronto Pearson International Airport, the successful candidate may work remotely with preference to those in Southern Ontario, Canada.\xa0<br><br></div><div><!--block-->Still think you have what it takes to thrive in our agile, high-growth, fast-paced environment?<br><br><strong>To be perfectly honest, we doubt it.<br></strong><br></div><div><!--block-->You're welcome to prove us wrong.</div><img src="https://remotive.com/job/track/2052049/blank.gif?source=public_api" alt=""/>'}

{'id': 2052162, 'url': 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/qa/automation-testing-2052162', 'title': 'Automation Testing', 'company_name': 'RiskInsight Consulting Pvt Ltd', 'company_logo': 'https://remotive.com/job/2052162/logo', 'category': 'QA', 'tags': ['java', 'python', 'agile', 'selenium'], 'job_type': 'full_time', 'publication_date': '2025-08-25T16:52:03', 'candidate_required_location': 'India', 'salary': '', 'description': '<p>·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 At least 5+ years development testing automation experience using automated tool such as Java / Python, Selenium, Genie framework. </p><p>·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 Develop and execute automated test scripts.</p><p>·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 Record and document defects in accordance with the project's requirement.</p><p>·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 Troubleshooting defects and provide fixes. </p><ul style=""> <li style="">Flexibility to deliver in both Agile &amp; Waterfall methodology.</li> <li style="">Experience working in a banking I.T. team preferred.</li> <li style="">Java Development: Core Java, JSON/XML </li> <li style="">Database: Oracle Database, SAP HANA SQL</li> <li style="">Middleware: IBM MQ, Queue and Topic</li> <li style="">IDE: Eclipse, IntelliJ</li> <li style="">Operating System: Linux (<a class="external" rel="nofollow">with shell scripting</a>), Windows</li> <li style="">Build tool: Maven.</li> <li style="">CI &amp; CD: Azure DevOps</li> <li style="">Confidence to face off to business users &amp; other stakeholders.</li> <li style="">Experience working in at least one full SDLC.</li> </ul><br><br><div class="h2">About the company</div><br><p>Riskinsight Consulting was established in India in September 2018 and it is a subsidiary of Unison Consulting. Its core purpose is to offer cutting-edge solutions in a wide range of areas. RiskInsight mission is to empower companies through our insurance and financial services.

We provide a wide range of risk management consulting services. Our experts are available to assist with credit, market and liquidity, insurance, regulatory risk management, statistical behavioral modeling, and regulatory risk management.

Consulting services are provided to help clients implement risk management systems and risk analytics systems for their institutions. We offer a complete range of services, including techno-functional consulting, system integration, business intelligence, information administration, and custom development IT solutions. Our clients are insured and financial institutions</p><img src="https://remotive.com/job/track/2052162/blank.gif?source=public_api" alt=""/>'}

